## Source ownership and steps

1. Root implements the public projection and capture in
   `tests/collab/fixture_support/native_stop_fixture.py` and
   `native_stop_channel.py`, with private component controls. Preserve literal
   cwd, optional null versus omission, source=userShell, real lifecycle timestamps
   and IDs. Account every complete original-connection frame from arm through
   closing, retain consecutive hash-linked raw prefixes, checkpoints from actual
   empty-buffer/nonreadable socket drain, real peer and monotonic cutoffs. Every
   unsupported owned tool or partial/gap/write/cap condition remains UNKNOWN.
2. Root implements a preflight-only immediate driver and source guards in this
   same fixture-support package. The independent A50 author implements static
   reconstruction, fresh whole-source equality, ObserverReady, channel reading,
   initial event/read/kernel conjunction and close request in `audit_support`.
   The independent reader must not import fixture-support or product-controller
   modules. The driver records actual bounded command/process/resource exits;
   it does not own the acceptance oracle or another queue. Both implementations
   use the pinned interface above; changes require a recorded shared ruling.
3. Freeze each immutable candidate before cold retention/materialization and
   independent source review. Profile the exact new sources and actual source
   guard/ready/closure path before admitting effects. Separate static preparation
   has its own <=120s/256MiB/zero-swap clock. Live operator and observer clocks
   each start at actual launch and remain <=120s. Source preparations count
   against those clocks. The proposed115.05s schedule is a bound to verify, not
   observed runtime evidence. Keep payload60s/128MiB, native timeout90s,
   capture<=95s, requests<=2s, frames<=128, ordinary checkpoints<=64, complete
   final checkpoint permitted as65, and combined fixture+channel output<=32MiB.
4. Only after exact source, timing, resource, layout and shared-writer admission,
   run one fresh non-managed E. Fresh sibling channel output is outside every
   original writer-scan/source/canonical/commonGit/observer root. No PID or FD
   exemptions. Static reconstruction precedes effects; fresh source guards and
   an actual acknowledged ObserverReady precede sole creation. Arm original
   connection before one shell request; the driver binds actual returned
   creation/invocation/channel/payload receipts before immediate observer reads.
   Initial <=5s interval requires real start event, all six native read methods
   and independent contemporaneous live kernel facts. Both terminal observations
   >=5s apart still require full terminal native item history, idle thread,
   terminal exact turn, absent goal, empty queue/handles, all known births gone,
   scope quiescence, no unexplained writers/gaps and unchanged source/caps.
   After retaining both observations the observer requests capture-only close;
   driver retains actual reaped recorder exit and the observer fully reconstructs
   sources again before sealing. Independent live reinspection is mandatory.

