## Recovery and source rulings

The compaction interruption did not reject implementation acceptance. On
recovery, canonical remains clean at the base above and the same native goal
is active. Partial root source is retained at `e1ebf9f`; independently authored
observer source continues from `e07de852`. No native or Kata effect was repeated.

Ruling: explicitly profile Python's installed startup files rather than admit a
site directory or change interpreter flags. Actual `sitecustomize.__file__` is
`/usr/lib/python3.11/sitecustomize.py`, resolving to
`/etc/python3.11/sitecustomize.py`. Both readonly profile executions must return
the same exact module name, observed alias, regular target and SHA256. The
raw helper source and command outputs, interpreter, flags, exit codes, dual
clocks and stdlib root are reopened before effects. A second alias to even the
same target refuses. This preserves the approved literal import closure and
records the machine's installed alias explicitly. Independent reader and root
fixture implementations share the data contract, never implementation code.

Root's42 private controls pass after observed alias/profile/static-binding
failures followed by corrections. These controls exercise exact-file admission,
retained raw command provenance, source mutations, wrong aliases, readiness,
fixed actor roles, kernel birth and failed-command retention. They are source
verification only; fresh-source independent review, actual profiles and live
E remain pending. Prior A/B/C/D UNKNOWN reports retain their original meaning.

Ruling: classify Python3.11's actual `typing.io` and `typing.re` class namespaces
through their defining literal stdlib `typing.py` body, exact parent export,
metaclass and exported-member identities. They have no `__file__` or `__spec__`;
do not pretend they are imported files or builtin modules. Record their owner
file/hash and classification separately. Unknown pathless objects, namespaces
and counterfeit aliases refuse. The independent staticv2 preparation exposed
this seam and remains UNKNOWN, with no native socket/thread/tool effects.
Root's prior unconditional pathless skip was too broad and is tightened by the
same data contract, using independently implemented code. New controls include
the actual full import inventory rather than only small mocked maps: bounded
RED had four failing tests (five assertions including namespace subcases), then
all46 root controls passed at256MiB/zero swap. The earlier unbounded RED also
hit the intentionally required readiness cgroup; the bounded reproduction
separates that environment refusal from the import defect. Source freeze,
independent review and a fresh actual static/live admission still follow.

The same review found that an arbitrary object with a forged `spec.origin`
string could claim builtin/frozen classification. Root's second bounded RED
reproduced both cases. Require an actual ModuleType/ModuleSpec, the installed
BuiltinImporter/FrozenImporter loader and a native registered builtin/frozen
name; retain the classification. The complete48-control suite passes after
this tightening. Its real-sys control initially overconstrained the whole
inventory to one entry, while Python legitimately loads `_io` during source
reads; it now asserts real `sys` classification without inventing a complete
one-entry import union. No native effects occurred during any component run.

R3.1 review then reproduced copied-owner, arbitrary-metaclass and wrong-definition
counterfeits against frozen `fadad077`; the raw owner-file hash alone attributed
those objects incorrectly. Their three root controls failed before correction.
Bind to the actual owner/namespace/member objects at trusted guard load and
verify definition names/qualnames plus metaclass method globals and literal
owner-code filename. All51 bounded controls pass after this correction. The
prior source candidate remains retained and is superseded for new admission;
its positive component suite never accepted runtime or ticket50.

An intermediate root commit `f562b961` was mistakenly made while two genuine
positive controls still failed: class name/qualname live in type slots rather
than `vars(class)`. Its suite failure and unadmitted source remain retained.
Read those attributes through `type.__getattribute__`; the complete51 tests
then pass (`8736fd`) at256MiB/zero swap before the corrected commit. This
corrects the source claim; it does not rewrite any prior test/report or admit
effects from the intermediate candidate.
